#: ../../library/time.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`time` --- time related functions"
msgstr ":mod:`time` --- fungsi-fungsi terkait waktu"

#: ../../library/time.rst:7
msgid ""
"The ``time`` module provides functions for getting the current time and "
"date, measuring time intervals, and for delays."
msgstr ""
"Modul ``time`` menyediakan fungsi untuk mendapatkan waktu dan tanggal saat "
"ini, mengukur interval waktu, serta untuk penundaan."

#: ../../library/time.rst:10
msgid ""
"**Time Epoch**: The Alif- and i.MX RT-based OpenMV Cams use the POSIX epoch "
"of 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC. The STM32-based OpenMV Cams use an epoch of "
"2000-01-01 00:00:00 UTC. The epoch year can be determined at runtime with "
"``gmtime(0)[0]``."
msgstr ""
"**Epoch Waktu**\\ : OpenMV Cam berbasis Alif dan i.MX RT menggunakan epoch "
"POSIX yaitu 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC. OpenMV Cam berbasis STM32 menggunakan "
"epoch 2000-01-01 00:00:00 UTC. Tahun epoch dapat ditentukan saat runtime "
"dengan ``gmtime(0)[0]``\\ ."

#: ../../library/time.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Maintaining actual calendar date/time**: This requires a Real Time Clock "
"(RTC). On the OpenMV Cam the system time is provided by the "
":class:`machine.RTC` object. The current calendar time may be set with "
"``machine.RTC().datetime(tuple)`` and is maintained by one of:"
msgstr ""
"**Mempertahankan tanggal/waktu kalender aktual**\\ : Ini memerlukan Real "
"Time Clock (RTC). Pada OpenMV Cam, waktu sistem disediakan oleh objek "
":class:`machine.RTC`\\ . Waktu kalender saat ini dapat diatur dengan "
"``machine.RTC().datetime(tuple)`` dan dipertahankan oleh salah satu dari:"

#: ../../library/time.rst:20
msgid "A backup battery (an optional component on some OpenMV Cams)."
msgstr "Baterai cadangan (komponen opsional pada beberapa OpenMV Cam)."

#: ../../library/time.rst:21
msgid ""
"A networked time protocol such as :mod:`ntptime` (requires a network "
"connection)."
msgstr ""
"Protokol waktu berbasis jaringan seperti :mod:`ntptime` (memerlukan koneksi "
"jaringan)."

#: ../../library/time.rst:23
msgid ""
"Setting it manually on each power-up. The RTC is then typically maintained "
"across soft resets, but is lost on power loss unless a backup battery is "
"fitted."
msgstr ""
"Mengaturnya secara manual setiap kali dinyalakan. RTC kemudian biasanya "
"dipertahankan saat soft reset, tetapi akan hilang saat kehilangan daya "
"kecuali jika baterai cadangan dipasang."

#: ../../library/time.rst:27
msgid ""
"If the calendar time is not maintained, the functions below that reference "
"the current absolute time will not behave as expected."
msgstr ""
"Jika waktu kalender tidak dipertahankan, fungsi-fungsi di bawah ini yang "
"merujuk ke waktu absolut saat ini tidak akan berperilaku sebagaimana "
"mestinya."

#: ../../library/time.rst:31
msgid "Functions"
msgstr "Fungsi"

#: ../../library/time.rst:36
msgid ""
"Convert the time *secs* expressed in seconds since the Epoch (see above) "
"into an 8-tuple which contains: ``(year, month, mday, hour, minute, second, "
"weekday, yearday)`` If *secs* is not provided or None, then the current time"
" from the RTC is used."
msgstr ""
"Mengonversi waktu *secs* yang dinyatakan dalam detik sejak Epoch (lihat di "
"atas) menjadi 8-tuple yang berisi: ``(year, month, mday, hour, minute, "
"second, weekday, yearday)`` Jika *secs* tidak diberikan atau None, maka "
"waktu saat ini dari RTC yang digunakan."

#: ../../library/time.rst:40
msgid ""
"The `gmtime()` function returns a date-time tuple in UTC, and `localtime()` "
"returns a date-time tuple in local time."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `gmtime()` mengembalikan tuple tanggal-waktu dalam UTC, dan "
"`localtime()` mengembalikan tuple tanggal-waktu dalam waktu lokal."

